---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">About the writer</div>
    <h1>Austin Martin.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An independent writer working across film, sports, culture and more.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="max-width:800px;padding-bottom:110px">
    <h2>Freelance and editorial.</h2>
    <p>
      I approach writing with an emphasis on research-based accuracy,
      reasoning, and depth of analysis, all while making it digestible for varying audiences.
      An understanding of broader context allows me to connect with readers through
      a balance engagement and clarity
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm interested in freelance and editorial opportunities that allow for investigation and analysis;
      specifically, ones offer an exploration through criticism, commentary, analysis, or longer-form essays.
    </p>
    <h2>About me and my writing process.</h2>
    <p>
      Film, sports, and culture are subjects of interest, but this space acts as an ongoing journal. I use
      it to refine my own thoughts, laying out current opinions on relevant subjects.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'd say thinking and writing are one in the same. Each paragraph is a subset of an idea,
      and while the writing process reveals it to be sound, requiring revision, or wrong. It's how you
      build a sound opinions worth discussion. My engineering day job consists of various experiments that investigate
      what is true physically. Writing represents an abstract form of the same process. Just as any problem
      must first be subdivided and structured in conceptualization, so too do questions of <em>why</em>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Further, each entry is a snapshot of where I stand at a given moment. A change in stance is definitely
      possible and even encouraged. The goal of these articles is to allow the reader a deeper understanding of
      the subject matter, while refining their own opinion both specifically and broadly.
    </p>
    <p>
      So, I document these thoughts, whether vague and abstract, or tangible and informative. I hope that
      these collection of thoughts may be useful; being accepted or proven wrong and left be. Thanks for your time.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/portfolio/">Browse selected work ↗</a>
  </section>
</Base>
